QuestGuidance.Register("en",150,{
[4769]="70070CD1\n1\tDestroy Orc supplies in Mokh Grazádh (total: 4)\030Defeat Baltmau skirmishers (total: 8)\030Defeat Baltmau stalkers (total: 6)\tYour mission is to travel to Mokh Grazádh to the west and thin the number of Orcs in the camp before they continue to attack Laivárth. If you can, destroy any supplies you come across as well.\n2\tDefeat the Baltmau overseer\tYour mission is to travel to Mokh Grazádh to the west and thin the number of Orcs in the camp before they continue to attack Laivárth. If you can, destroy any supplies you come across as well.\n",
[4770]="7001B1F6\n1\tFree Elves from the cocoons (total: 4)\tThe ensnared Elves may be found in the nests of the spiders to the north of Ivorel's camp. Miluimil has asked you to set forth to free his ensnared companions.\n2\tTalk to Miluimil at Ivorel's camp\tMiluimil is at Ivorel's camp, south of the spider-nests. You should speak with Miluimil and tell him that the scouts have been freed.\n",
[4771]="700606BD\n1\tFind the road to Eitheldir\tThe road to Eitheldir is in the northern Angle. You should look for the road to Eitheldir.\n2\tSearch for Merileg\tMerileg is located near the ruins of Eitheldir, in the northern Angle. Elladan has asked you to deliver a letter of introduction to Merileg.\n",
[4772]="70043B4B\n1\tTalk to Bingo in the outpost of Etheburg, on the edge of the Brown Lands\tThe outpost of Etheburg is on the edge of the Brown Lands, beyond the Rushgore. Bingo has decided to take matters into his own hands, and wants to investigate the Brown Lands.\n2\tEasterlings can be found throughout the Brown Lands, and Bingo has asked you to fight them in order to help the men of Stangard.\t\n3\tDefeat Easterlings in the Brown Lands (11/12)\tEasterlings can be found throughout the Brown Lands, and Bingo has asked you to fight them in order to help the men of Stangard.\n4\tBring the secret orders to Bingo in Etheburg, on the edge of the Brown Lands\tBingo is in the outpost of Etheburg, on the edge of the Brown Lands. You found a parchment apparently containing orders for the Easterlings that describe a secret attack on an outpost that sounds like Stangard.\n5\tBring the secret orders to Sabert at the east-gate of Stangard\tSabert is at the east-gate of the outpost of Stangard. You have found some worrisome orders to the Easterlings, and Bingo wants you to show them to Sabert at Stangard.\n6\tTalk to Bingo at the east-gate of Stangard and prepare for the Easterling offensive\tSabert is at the east-gate of the outpost of Stangard. Sabert has had a change of heart, now that you have shown him proof of the Easterling plan, and now he wants you to help him with the defences of Stangard.\n7\tTalk to Langhár within Stangard\tLanghár is in the upper courtyard of Stangard. You and your allies successfully defended Stangard from the Easterling attack.\n8\tTalk to Bingo within Stangard\tBingo is in the upper courtyard of Stangard. You and your allies successfully defended Stangard from the Easterling attack.\n",
[4773]="70056942\n1\tReach Level 130\tMablung is awaiting your return in Echad Taerdim, the Ranger camp in Cirith Ungol. You should report to Mablung when you are able.\n2\tTalk to Mablung\tMablung is awaiting your return in Echad Taerdim, the Ranger camp in Cirith Ungol. You should report to Mablung when you are able.\n3\tTalk to Celeborn inside Torech Ungol\tCeleborn and the Rangers have set up a small staging camp inside Torech Ungol. You should find the camp and report to Celeborn.\n4\tEnter the Remmorchant\tThe time has come to enter the Remmorchant. You should enter the Remmorchant with a raid group ready via the Instance Finder panel.\n5\tDefeat Bratha Tasakh, Lady of Many Venoms\tThe chieftain of the Ungoledain blocks your path deeper into the Remmorchant. You should defeat Bratha Tasakh, Lady of Many Venoms.\n6\tProceed deeper into the Remmorchant\tBratha Tasakh and her Ungoledain have been defeated. You should press further into the Remmorchant.\n7\tDefeat Gragarag of the Queensbrood\030Defeat Guruthang of the Queensbrood\030Defeat Gamnagol of the Queensbrood\030Defeat Thossulun the Massive\tThe mighty children of Shelob block your path forward. You should defeat the Queensbrood and Thossulun the Massive.\n8\tProceed deeper into the Remmorchant\tThossulun and the Queensbrood have fallen, finally stemming the tide of spiders and gredbyg. You should press further into the Remmorchant.\n9\tDefeat Rûkhor the Pale Herald\tRûkhor the Pale Herald has unveiled his nefarious plot! You should defeat Rûkhor the Pale Herald before he succeeds in his plan!\n10\tDefeat Shelob\tThe time has come to face Shelob within the Remmorchant. You should defeat Shelob.\n11\tTalk to Celeborn\tShelob has been defeated at last. You should talk to Celeborn.\n",
[4774]="700718F2\n1\tTalk to Halshûm\tYou have been instructed by the guard at the entrance to Khanâg Gur to introduce yourself to someone called the 'Khanda-mashár'. You should speak to Halshûm.\n",
[4775]="700266EE\n1\tCollect rubbings within Haudh Eärendur (total: 8)\tHaudh Eärendur is within the Way of Kings, west of the Rangers' camp. Nimbellas has asked you to take rubbings of engravings from the tombs within Haudh Eärendur.\n2\tTalk to Nimbellas in the Way of Kings\tNimbellas is at the Ranger-camp in the Way of Kings. Nimbellas will be eager to examine the rubbings you collected.\n",
[4776]="70025A36\n1\tDiscover the first entranceway\030Discover the second entranceway\030Discover the third entranceway\030Discover the fourth entranceway\030Discover the fifth entranceway\tBarad Tharsír is south-east of the colossus on the east bank of the Brandywine River. Daerol asked you to scout the ruins of Barad Tharsír and report back on what you find.\n2\tTalk to Daerol at the colossus\tDaerol is at the colossus, north-west of Barad Tharsír. Daerol will be very interested to hear what you learned about the doors of Barad Tharsír.\n",
